findings.body:
`testManageOnlyOneClient` makes several changes to `myclient`, the client that `realmAdminClient` authenticates with:
- removes `defaultClientScopes.get(1)` (index into an unordered list, so the removed scope is nondeterministic, possibly `basic` or `roles`);
- re-adds it as optional;
- renames the client.

None of this is restored. Other tests in the class reuse the same realm and client, so results can depend on test execution order and on which scope happened to be removed. `testMapRolesAndCompositesOnlyOneClient` similarly leaves created client roles and a role mapping on myadmin. Clean these up or mark the realm dirty.
